[9.4136, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b[?25l\u001b[0m\u001b[?7l\u001b[0m\u001b[J\u001b[0mVous >\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\n\r\r\n\r\r\n\r\r\n\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[0m \b\u001b[7A\u001b[7C\u001b[?7h\u001b[0m\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h"]
[10.5648, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[?7l\u001b[7D\u001b[0mVous > Use web_fetch on https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html . Based on the returned page, st\r\u001b[109Ca\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[0m       te whether pytest supports ordinary Python assert statements for our cart tests. Answer in one short s\r\u001b[109Ce\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[0m       ntence and include the source URL. No JSON. Do not search again.\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\n\r\r\n\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[0m \u001b[5A\u001b[70C\u001b[?7h\u001b[0m\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h"]
